what are my favorite work life hacks so  I recently did a video about my favorite  YouTube channels and the ones that I  subscribed to there aren't that many the  ones that I kind of watch all the time  and one of my loyal YouTube followers  Neil pol shook wrote in to ask me Evan I  love the Tim Ferriss channel that you  you added what are some of your favorite  work life hacks and that's a that's a  tough question for me because for the  past I don't know ten years I've been  doing a ton of experiments on myself and  my productivity on things that that I  like and don't know what works I'm  constantly changing around my schedule  and the things that I do and I live kind  of a weird lifestyle I guess compared to  most people you know I wear barefoot  shoes I use a stand-up desk I go  snowboard in the middle the afternoon  and we go all over the place I'm in the  office three hours a day from Monday to  Thursday it's kind of uh it's different  I guess and it's come from years of kind  of trial and error wasn't just one day I  woke up and tried to do all these things  all at once I don't use my cell phone my  phone number isn't on my business card  or my website that's another big one  anyway so some of the ones I've had kind  of the biggest impact for me personally  I'm gonna share three of them and  hopefully this helps answer the question  this one made me think Neil it made me  think you making me do some hard work  today  the first one was when I first started  delegating I remember with my first  company my software company I always  kind of had in my head that I had to do  everything myself or my partners would  do it but not the idea of having  somebody come on to help me and the  first person I brought on board was for  one hour a day I couldn't afford to hire  a full-time person and I was growing  increasingly frustrated with all the  repetitive tasks that I had to do and it  was like I can't focus on the bigger  stuff because I'm so crunched down and  doing these stupid things and I felt  like somebody could do this better than  me and my my aha moment I guess came  when I realized that I don't have to  hire somebody full-time which I couldn't  afford I can hire somebody for a little  bit amount of time and it was a guy I  knew his name was Rob first guy hired  and it was for one hour day and I was  doing a bunch of database work that I  hated and I gave it to him and he was  better at it faster at it than me he got  a lot more done in that hour than I  could and it freed up an hour of time  for me to go and do more stuff with my  business and that was just a little  improvement I guess to my life at the  time but it just set me on this course  because now I hate doing things that are  repetitive tasks and as quickly as  possible as soon as I get bored or  something I'm handing it off to someone  else to do or maybe killing a project  but but I am NOT stuck in repetitive  task mode and being held back from doing  things that I need to do to grow my  business and that's just I don't know it  kills your creativity it kills your  productivity when you're stuck doing  repetitive things that you hate over and  over and over again so ever since that  one small event of hiring Rob for one  hour a day I've been looking to make my  workflow easier and more efficient by  hiring people  the second was chunking my time and this  one came to me as a result of reading  the 4-hour workweek and the idea here is  anything that you do multiple times per  week do once per week you do things  multiple times per day do once per day  the first biggest improvement thing was  email I used to be the guy who have  super fast on email answering right away  you know I get that alert when it came  into my Outlook at the time and I would  go and answer it right away and people  would respond how fast I was and it was  great but every time I went to check my  email because something new came in it  distracted me from something else and I  ended up not getting my other tasks done  I would just basically be on email all  day and it just killed my creativity and  my productivity and so what I did was I  said okay I'm gonna do email I started  it twice a day and then I went down to  once a day and now I don't even have a  set time for email I do it when I'm not  doing anything else and just unloading  that was a huge relief for me it freed  up so much of my time cuz think about  when you get interrupted at least for me  it takes to another like half an hour to  get back into the zone I was in and so I  that elimination lets me just focus  hardcore on set tasks and it really  helped me I've applied that chunking to  everything I do in my schedule so I do  my videos on a Wednesday so I I speak  with my media coach Wednesday morning  today's Wednesday  I spoke with genja this morning and then  sit down and do my videos and so I'm  kind of I'm in video mode I'm thinking  video when I'm in the shower I'm  thinking what I'm gonna talk about my  video washing the hair what's gonna  happen my video and I'm ready to do back  to back to back to back to back videos  and it's great because setting up the  video camera and the microphone and  everything getting the questions ready  takes time and so I don't have to do  that each time I do it once per week and  I'm done on Thursdays I do my meetings  and interviews and my radio show and I'm  kind of in that zone that day so I'm not  worried about admin tasks or anything  else related to the business I'm just  meeting people talking to people and  it's easy to go from one meeting to the  next to the next to the next hangout on  Google and whatever it is that I'm doing  again I found before if I had meetings  all over the place  half an hour before meeting I found like  my productivity was was shot like I  can't start something new because I know  I have a meeting coming up in 30 minutes  so I'm just gonna do little tasks right  and I just found that happen too much  but when you have back to back to back  to back meetings it kind of just puts  you in that zone and helps you flow  through without being distracted by  what's happening next and then on Monday  and Tuesday I'll do more of my  solitary work or project work so if I'm  writing my newsletter or writing an  article or doing something that I can  just do by myself  you know maybe I won't shave that day  whatever I feel like doing I'm kind of  in that zone and I find to just send  that my week that way really helps me  and then the third thing that I discover  and this was the hardest one for me to  break I think was was flow and momentum  so one thing I found with my chunk  schedule was like I was getting a lot  more done right by chunking my time and  limiting the email to certain parts of  the day I got so much more done during  the day but then I sometimes found  myself wanting to continue on on  something and having to stop because I  fell outside my chunk so I would chunk  my day into 90-minute segments I found I  would I would work best in Sprint's of  90 minutes then take a break then  something else for 90 minutes and  knowing that I only had 90 minutes kind  of forces me to go crazy fast but I  found just sometimes when I was working  on a project that I wanted more time I  was really feeling this idea I was  really feeling it and so I was in flow  and I found if I came back to it the  next day I feel like what was I thinking  about yesterday what was that project I  was working on I don't I would write  notes I don't remember what they mean  anymore I know if that happens to you  guys it happened to me and so I would  break my chunking schedule only if I was  in the flow and because the stuff that  you create when you're in flow is so  critical so important that's like the  big picture life-changing stuff you have  to keep going on it and you don't want  to fool yourself and say you know I'm in  the flow on these emails this is great  I'm answering everything so quickly  that's not what I'm talking about I'm  talking about the big ideas the things  that will change you and your business  for the better you get those things you  don't wait on them  don't don't wait on it and then you come  back tomorrow and it's it's like the  idea is not quite there anymore take  action right away I learn the rules of  chunking and then and then I know when  to break them with momentum all right so  those are the three things that that in  terms of work life  tax productivity have helped me the most  so again delegating even for one hour a  day and just taking the stuff off your  plate that you don't need to be doing  then chunking your time down so anything  you do multiple times you're doing it  once at a time and just set that time  aside so you can be excellent at it and  then momentum when you're in the flow  when you're feeling the momentum that's  the most important thing that you need  to work work and focus on for that day  and forget everything else that you're  doing because you're gonna you have to  stay in that zone I've created a series  of Zuka guides that go through exactly  how I break down those processes how to  automate eliminate delegate use flow  just from my experience as an  entrepreneur it's basically time  management for entrepreneur and a series  of guides so that could be super helpful  for you but those are my three I guess  most impactful most powerful things I  discovered that shaped how I view the  world as an entrepreneur and how I'm  more productive in my life so thank you  for the great question Neal for those of  you guys watching you like the video  please give it a thumbs up below you  have a question if you want to share a  productivity or life hack that's worked  well for you please leave it in the  comments below and if you want to see  more videos like this you can click on  my face subscribe to the channel and  you'll see more thank you guys so much  and I'll see you soon
 

